window.EN={"1":"Having escaped the burning Leonster Castle and barely survived, Prince Leif,","2":"together with Finn, the knight who protects him, and his daughter Nanna,","3":"[evading] Thracia, and the one that defeated Thracia and seized control of northern Thracia,","4":"the great western power, the Grannvale Empire, and other pursuers,","5":"Ulster,","6":"drifted from place to place, Tahra among them,","7":"and washed up in a small village called Fiana, near the sea in the east of the Thracian region.","8":"It was an independent village governed by a swordswoman named Eyvel,","9":"where brawny men took up arms and protected the neighboring villages from bandits.","10":"Eyvel welcomed them gladly.","11":"Leif, deepening his friendships with the village youths who gathered out of admiration for her,","12":"gradually grew toward adulthood.","13":"And then, Gran Year 776...","14":"Well? Have you found the prince?","15":"No, sir. We have searched every corner of the village, but we have not found him yet.","16":"You fool! What are you dawdling for?","17":"There is no doubt that a survivor of the Kingdom of Leonster is hiding in this village.","18":"Squeeze the villagers and make them spit out where he is!","19":"Yes, sir. Of course, we are doing so.","20":"However, it seems to be true that he is not in this village.","21":"The villagers say that the prince and his companions went with the Fiana Freeblades to help a village attacked by pirates.","22":"Fiana Freeblades? What is that...?","23":"It seems this village was originally a bandits' den.","24":"A dozen or so years ago, a traveling mercenary named Eyvel subdued the bandits and settled in as its ruler,","25":"and now they call themselves a volunteer army and are said to protect the nearby villages. I hear she is quite a skilled woman...","26":"Hmm... That is a bit of a nuisance.","27":"There is no need to worry.","28":"We have captured Eyvel's daughter and are holding her hostage.","29":"We also captured the daughter of the knight Finn, the prince's bodyguard. With this, they won't be able to resist.","30":"Oh? Well done, for you.","31":"Very well. I will take the girls back to Munster.","32":"You stay in the village and wait for the rebels to return.","33":"When the prince comes back, be sure to capture him!","34":"Yes, sir. Leave it to me.","35":"Someone! Bring the girls here!","36":"Girl, what is your name?","37":"Hmph...","38":"Heh. A strong will has its own charm.","39":"And the other one...","40":"Oh, so you are Finn's daughter. I hear your mother is a princess of the Kingdom of Nordion.","41":"Blood will tell, indeed. Even out here in the backwoods, you have not lost your refinement.","42":"......","43":"Heh heh heh, an unexpected souvenir. Very well, let us return to Munster.","44":"Weissman, I leave the rest to you!","45":"Yes, sir!","46":"I wonder what's wrong. Something seems off...","47":"Lady Eyvel, I'll go take a look. Please wait a moment.","48":"Lady Eyvel, the village is full of imperial soldiers. It seems it was attacked while we were away...","49":"What!? Damn it, those imperial bastards, pulling a stunt like this!","50":"Lady Eyvel, let's hurry to the village!","51":"Calm down, Osian. If we go back to the village without any preparation, the imperial soldiers will just turn the tables on us.","52":"Halvan, how can you be so calm!? The village is under attack!","53":"Halvan is right. Osian, calm down a little.","54":"Lord Leif, it seems the Empire has found us out.","55":"I'm sorry, but this is where we part.","56":"While we draw the imperial soldiers' attention, please flee as far away as you can.","57":"Finn, you go with the prince too...","58":"Eyvel!","59":"Nanna is in the village. We can't run away on our own.","60":"I will get Lady Nanna back. Please don't worry, Lord Leif.","61":"No, that's not it. I'm not running anymore. I've decided that.","62":"Finn, what about you? Are you fine with putting the prince in danger?","63":"The prince has turned fifteen. He is already of an age to decide his own fate.","64":"As one of his retainers, I will follow the prince's will.","65":"I see, fifteen... So that's why you brought him along on the pirate hunt.","66":"Understood. If Finn says so, I have no objection.","67":"...I don't really get it, but if you're done talking, let's get going already!","68":"Yes, but be careful. Imperial soldiers they may be, but the low-ranking ones are civilians who were conscripted by force.","69":"If you can, capture them without killing them, take their weapons, and then release them. Understood?","70":"But it's fine to rough them up enough that they can't fight back, right? Otherwise we'll be the ones getting done in.","71":"Well, yes, that's true, but don't rough them up so much that you kill them.","72":"You especially need to be careful, Osian.","73":"Tch, so you don't trust me?","74":"Then let's go. Everyone, fight in a way that does honor to the name of the Fiana Freeblades!","75":"Pops, it's already started.","76":"This is bad.","77":"Even Eyvel can't handle imperial soldiers... Let's hurry.","78":"Oh, man, what a mess...","79":"Dagdar!? You came.","80":"Oh, Eyvel. I'm glad you're safe.","81":"For the imperial army to come all the way out to the backwoods, there must be quite a reason. It's about that child after all...","82":"Yes. The truth is, that child is the prince of the fallen Kingdom of Leonster.","83":"I sheltered him on my own judgment. I'm sorry for hiding it.","84":"I figured it was something like that.","85":"Well, fine. If I get to fight the imperial army, I have no complaints.","86":"Hey, if it isn't Tanya. What are you doing?","87":"Osian!? Can't you tell by looking? I came all this way to help you!","88":"\"Came to help\"? We're not so pathetic that we need help from you.","89":"Go on, kids should run along home.","90":"K-kid!? You're the kid here!!","91":"I'll go home without being told! Who'd come to a place like this because they wanted to, you idiot!","92":"Little Miss Mareeta and little Miss Nanna were taken away by the imperial soldiers. Please hurry and rescue them.","93":"Oh, that's right. Take this magic bracelet with you. I think it'll come in handy.","94":"But just carrying it won't do, mind. You have to actually use it.","95":"Everyone, you came back! Thank goodness...","96":"Please, save the village... save the village!","97":"This... is a vulnerary. Please use it.","98":"No, it's fine. Compared to the kindness we've received from Lady Eyvel, this is nothing...","99":"Weapons are expensive things, so poor folk like us can't buy them.","100":"It's a sorry thing to say, but I suppose there's nothing for it but to capture enemies and take theirs.","101":"Look, just like this, I swiped one from an imperial soldier myself.","102":"Though I did it while the fellow was snoring. Ho ho ho.","103":"If junk like this will do, I'll give it to you.","104":"If you don't need it, just sell it off at the item shop over there. It'll fetch a little money.","105":"Oh, big brother! I'll give you something good. Won't this be useful?","106":"? ...What's this axe?","107":"Looks like a good axe, doesn't it?","108":"The other day when I was walking in the hills out back, I got it from a weird lady who came out of a spring.","109":"But I don't think I really need it, so you use it, big brother.","110":"Have you seen big brother Halvan? I wonder if he's doing well...","111":"Osian, are you taking things seriously? Don't you go being a burden on Lady Eyvel.","112":"Damn old man. I've had enough lectures.","113":"You delinquent son, only your mouth has grown up.","114":"Well, fine. Here, this is what you came for, isn't it?","115":"Oh, thanks. I just can't settle down unless it's this axe.","116":"Honestly, what a blunderer.","117":"I've never heard of a guy who forgets his own weapon when he goes off to battle.","118":"Tch. That's why I said I've had enough lectures.","119":"Hmph. Now hurry up and go help Lady Eyvel!","120":"I'll do that without being told.","121":"Where's that Osian fooling around? That good-for-nothing!","122":"Nanna! Mareeta! Where are you!? Answer me!!","123":"It seems the two of them were taken away by Baron Raydrik.","124":"What!? Then, to Munster?","125":"Probably. He must intend to use them as hostages. Just the sort of thing Raydrik would think of...","126":"Ugh... Eyvel, let's go after them. Let's save them!","127":"But, Lord Leif, you...","128":"They were captured in my place, Eyvel.","129":"I'm not a child anymore. I hate living at the cost of someone else's sacrifice!","130":"...Understood. Then we will set out tomorrow morning.","131":"It will be a hard journey. Please rest well tonight.","132":"Nanna! Mareeta! Where are you!? Answer me!!","133":"Oh, Lord Leif. So you are safe.","134":"Forgive us. Even though we were with her, Lady Nanna...","135":"Nanna? What happened to Nanna?","136":"The imperial soldiers took her away.","137":"Lady Mareeta did her best to let at least Lady Nanna escape,","138":"but in the end even Lady Mareeta was caught...","139":"So where were they taken?","140":"Well, as for that...","141":"Oh! Come to think of it, a soldier outside was saying \"back to Munster\" or some such.","142":"Munster, then. I understand. It's all right, don't worry.","143":"Nanna, Mareeta, and Eyvel too... I'll get them all back!","144":"If you kill me, the hostages' lives are forfeit. Do you understand that!?","145":"Damn it... You people will regret this...","146":"D-damn it! Y-you'll remember this!"};
